nvelope  and the membrane  followed by the presence of a nuclear  capsule inside in which the single  standard rna is contained  it also contains a replicase enzyme  orf1a1b which is of a fused orf thus it  has six functional orfs  which go in the order of five dash to  three dash  also several orfs encoding accessory  proteins were observed  coming to the genome sequence identity  analysis of the virus it was showed that  it shares maximum identity of up to 90  amongst all animals with bad virus  and coming to the viral taxonomy it says  79 identity with sars covet and 50 with  mercy ov  also initially it is the spike protein  of the virus that is responsible for its  antigenicity and recognition by the  ace which is the angiotensin converting  enzyme to receptors  the virus does enters the alveolar  epithelial cell with the lungs and it is  it is followed by replication and  subsequent migration down to the airways  which can progress to the lungs and the  respiratory the respiratory organs thus  it causes respiratory distress and  discomfort in patients  thus to uh  to  to analyze and develop therapeutic  targets against the cobit 19 disease it  is very important that we understand the  transcriptomic changes that are  associated with the clinical progression  of the disease  so with the a with the same aim a  pipeline was developed and all the  stages were carried out on the t bio  server of the  t bio server and various interactive and  interesting pipelines were followed that  gave very graphic results  the data set number  gse17867 was obtained from the jio  website  144 samples had progressive data which  means that  at day zero they had either asymptomatic  or mild disease  and at day five the disease had  progressed either to the moderate or  severe disease  the rest of the patients had only data  for one of the days amongst day zero and  day 5 and thus they were excluded from  the study  the q score of all the sequenced  uh sequence genes and and the ngs 