h that the day  zero samples  were observed in the second and the  third quadrant and the day five samples  were observed in the first and the first  fourth quadrant  in the graph  thus the pcs scatter plot says that  significantly differentially expressed  genes are observed in the mild and  progressive stage patients and the  significant difference is observed on  the pca plot by the segregation of the  plots in various models  the immunological profiling of severe to  moderate kubernetes patients is  characterized by increasing order of  density of the regulation of pathways  such as jack strat pathways cytokine  receptor interaction and hematopoietic  linings with which leads to pronounced t  cell lymphopenia  also it is important that host antiviral  responses are innate in nature and  involves cytokines and interferon  induced proteins  the key differentially expressed genes  that modulate the significant pathways  in genes are identified to various  degrees in moderate mild severe and  asymptomatic over 19 patients  all this can also lead to  the development of a hyper inflammatory  state  and  when the viral load was correlated with  the disease severity it showed no  significant correlation which also  states that uh even mild patients or  patients that have asymptomatic in my  disease are highly highly infectious  thus it is important to  to have steps like social distancing and  hygiene even in across all patients and  even non-infected people by varying of  mass etc to prevent the spread of the  same  so to conclude with i would like to say  that the transcriptomic analysis showed  that the transcriptome of stars covered  two infected cells reflected the  interplay between host and virus which  can provide valuable insights into  mechanisms underlying sars govid  infection development and the copenhagen  disease progression  the viral infection triggers a  large-scale host immune response and  leads to the up regulation and down  regulation of in hundred